   Air Pollution, Rhodes, GREECE, 2004},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {It is well known that vehicles contribute to harmful air pollution in
   busy towns and cities. The correlation between traffic, air pollution
   and meteorological parameters in the city of Athens has been examined in
   this work.
   Approximately 3,000,000 vehicles circulate on the roads of Athens, of
   which the vast majority are private cars. Car occupancy is reaching only
   1.4 passengers/vehicle, which leads to chaotic traffic conditions and
   health problems due to near ground air pollution.
   In order to have an overview of the impact of traffic on the urban air
   pollution level two main tasks were performed in the frame of a European
   Union project a) Collation and analysis of already existing air
   pollution, traffic and meteorological data and b) On field measurements
   on two typical roads (street canyon and open road) and on an urban
   background site. Traffic measurements were carried out during summer
   period (13-23 July 2003) while air pollution and meteorological
   parameters were recorded on a continuous basis. Spatial and temporal
   variations as well as the correlation of the above parameters have been
   examined. The above mentioned work led to interesting results regarding
   the way that the urban environment affects the pollution level and the
   dissemination of the air pollutants in the city area.},
