   Catalunya, Dept Interior; CSIC},
Abstract = {Historical records are an important source for the evaluation of climate
   development and the frequency of extreme events. Documentary sources
   provide direct information about climatic parameters and their impact on
   society. Their high temporal resolution is of special benefit for the
   examination of natural disasters, such as large floods. With their
   direct effect on human life, these events have always captivated
   people's attention. Schemes for source criticism take into account the
   subjective nature of written sources. Applying qualitative-hermeneutic
   as well as quantitative-statistic approaches, and implementing modern
   gauging station data, long time series for the flood development in
   various Central European river systems have been reconstructed. The
   recently acquired data reach back to the year 1300. They allow us to
   identify new structures, for example a marked peak in the early 15(th)
   century for the Lower Rhine system.},
