Abstract = {This paper aims to uncover the creative music potentials of disabled
   youths in Malaysia. Often perceived as petty street musicians, who
   perform to earn subsistence living, their talent remains hidden, without
   avenues to become full-time professionals. This research attempts to
   bridge this gap by proposing an architectural intervention that
   functions entirely as a disabled-friendly building as well as enhances
   the affinity of music creation and learning. The spatial educative
   environment created focuses on musical rehabilitation for youths of the
   visually impaired, hearing-impaired and physically handicapped. The
   centre addresses their plight appreciatively, fusing their disability
   and talent in a unique symphony. (C) 2012 Published by Elsevier B.V.
