Abstract = {The national mass housing policies are currently being scrutinised on
   affordability and quality of life. The consideration of a better
   neighbourhood design is currently only evident in curvilinear and
   organic planning designs of neighbourhoods such as the cul-de-sac. The
   objective of this paper is to identify concepts of the cul-de-sac
   neighbourhoods and the community's social cohesion through a critical
   review of available literature within the framework settings of a
   Malaysian pluralistic neighbourhood. The paper is anticipated to lead to
   methodological assessment processes of the physical environment and
   neighbourhoods as well as expand existing contextual knowledge of the
   Malaysian cul-de-sac neighbourhoods. (C) 2012 Published by Elsevier B.V.
