   AND THE POLITICIANS},
Year = {1998},
Pages = {33-35},
Note = {Annual Meeting of the Ecological-Society-of-Australia, TOWNSVILLE,
   AUSTRALIA, 1996},
Organization = {Ecol Soc Australia; CSIRO Div Wildlife \& Ecol; Kings Pk \& Bot Garden;
   Absett Airlines \& Traveland},
Abstract = {Tour operators possibly educate more people about Australia's ecology
   than all ecology lecturers combined. In addition to this, a case could
   be made that much of tourism in Australia, from international marketing
   th rough to taking a nature-based tour, is based on the country's
   ecology. The tourism industry and tourists themselves should be major
   promoters of ecological research and users of its results. Yet one of
   the most obvious deficiencies of tourism agents and operators is the
   level of education and communication skills. Misinformation on
   biodiversity, ecology and management is particularly common.
   The main goal of communicating ecology is conservation of ecosystems. To
   communicate ecology effectively, passion and politics must be put back
   into the equation.},
