   JUN 25-27, 2024},
Organization = {University of Salento},
Abstract = {Transporting plays a crucial role in global efforts to climate change
   mitigation climate, as it is a significant contributor to greenhouse gas
   emissions. As climate change increasingly impacts the Mediterranean as
   well, the region's approach to transport policies becomes a crucial
   instrument in achieving sustainability and resilience. In order to
   connect the two main such as transport climate change, various policy
   frameworks have been developed. However, so far, no consistent framework
   addresses these two areas in an integrated approach. Therefore, this
   study explores the intersection of transport policies, urban
   development, and climate changer mitigations, through a methodology of
   bibliographic analyses. The study highlights the unimportance of
   understanding the Mediterranean's complex transportation dynamics.
   Moreover, it will review the specific drivers and barriers influencing
   the formulation and execution of integrated transport policies in the
   Mediterranean. These factors, starting from economic considerations and
   technological advancements to the diverse political, social, and
   environments lie through the region. In conclusion, this review
   highlights the relevance of the importance of adopting an integrated
   approach to transport policies within the Mediterranean context, through
   a systematic literature review of articles.},
