   Thinktank - Handsbrain Educ; SE Univ State Key Lab Bioelect; Chinese Soc
   Biomed Elect},
Abstract = {Emotional expressivity scale, emotion regulation questionnaire, and mood
   scale were administered to 370 college students. This study investigated
   the characteristics of emotional expressivity, emotion regulation and
   mood of different ethnic college students. The results showed that girls
   had more emotional expressivity, boys had more positive emotion, boys
   used more restraint emotion regulation strategies than girls; Han
   nationality students used more emotion regulation strategies than
   minority students, and minority students had higher negative mood than
   Han nationality students; Compared with other nationalities, Tibetan
   students had higher negative emotional expressivity, higher emotional
   intensity, and higher negative mood.},
