   Explos Sci \& Technol},
Abstract = {Based on investigation on waste disposal of several typical construction
   projects, the project differences were analyzed on the waste amount and
   components, and the components and the proportions of construction
   wastes were related to the structure types, the construction ages, local
   customs, resources and economic level, etc. The increasing environmental
   impact of construction wastes was discussed in following aspects:
   wasting land, damaging city appearance, polluting soil, water and
   atmosphere. The environmental impact of construction wastes is permanent
   and accumulated, and the components are increasing diversified, so, the
   secondary contaminations are also increasing severe. The disposal
   advices were given on the aspects of reducing, resources and
   eco-friendship of construction wastes. The necessary measures are
   following: enhancing urban planning and building design level, utilizing
   environment friendly materials and construction technology and
   increasing disposal and recycling rates of construction wastes.},
