   06-10, 1993},
Abstract = {Artificial intelligence (AI) has received an explosion of interest
   during the last 5 years in various fields. There is no longer any
   question that expert systems and neural networks will be of central
   importance for developing the next generation of more intelligent
   geographic information systems. Such knowledge-based geographic
   information systems will play an especially key role in spatial decision
   and policy analysis related to issues such as environmental monitoring
   and management, land use planning, motor vehicle navigation, and
   distribution logistics. This paper sketches briefly the major
   characteristics of conventional geographic information systems, and then
   looks at some of the potentials of AI principles and techniques in a GIS
   environment where emphasis is laid on expert systems and artificial
   neural networks technologies and techniques.},
