   Adm Bur; Natl Nat Sci Fdn China; NPC, Legislat Dept Nat \& Environm
   Resources Comm},
Abstract = {In and and semi - and regions, droughts are a common feature due to
   uncertainty in rainfall and the runoff and thereby the soil loss is more
   during heavy rainfall monsoon days. This is due to overgrazing, illicit
   felling of trees, faulty agronomic practices, shifting cultivation of
   crops in the Eastern region, etc. Hence a need was felt to improve and
   sustain water resources in this fragile eco - system. Therefore the
   Government of India initiated watershed development programme during
   1983 - 1984 and has been continuing since then with an annual budget
   allocation of over Rs. 1,000 crores for conserving soil and water
   resources and improve vegetation status of watershed. WDP improved the
   soil and water resources effectively in India in addition to improving
   vegetation.},
