   International-Society-for-the-Study-of-Behavioural-Development, nanjing,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 15-17, 2009},
Organization = {Int Soc Study Behav Dev; SE Univ, Key Lab Child Dev \& Learning Sci;
   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {By doing behavioral experiments under a combined paradigm of emotion
   priming and implicit association test, we investigated how neutral nouns
   primed by emotional adjectives. At first, we assessed and selected
   materials. Then, the subjects were asked to response according to our
   experiment design. Finally, we analyzed the reaction lime and correct
   ratio. From the results we found (1) under compatible condition, the
   reaction lime of positive emotion was significantly shorter than that of
   the negative emotion. Meanwhile, under positive condition, the reaction
   time under imcompatible condition was significantly longer than that
   under compatible condition; (2) Under compatible condition, the correct
   ratio of positive emotion was significantly higher-than that of the
   negative emotion. Nevertheless, the results reversed under imcompatible
   condition. Under emotion condition, the correct ratio of compatible
   condition was higher than that of the imcompatible condition.},
