   SPAIN, SEP 24-26, 1991},
Abstract = {The importance of public attitudes in the adoption of reclamation
   projects has been recognized for some time.  We know that people's
   perceptions and opinions are forces that can mean the difference between
   survival or extinction....success or failure.  This is a reality that
   must be recognized in the way we plan and implement a reuse program.
   While there is no ``fool-proof{''} guarantee of success, a sound
   pro-active communication and education program is essential.  This paper
   will give some guidelines that you can use to develop a planned
   communication program that can help you reach technical objectives,
   obtain public support, and win acceptance for your program.},
