   ENVIRONMENT},
Year = {2000},
Pages = {95-99},
Note = {International Symposium on Hydrogeology and the Environment (HE 2000),
   WUHAN, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 17-21, 2000},
Organization = {China Univ Geosci},
Abstract = {Groundwater is the only source of water supply for the more than 140,000
   inhabitants of Salamanca, in Central Mexico. There are evidences of
   organic compounds and metals pollution in the shallow aquifer. 1
   polluted urban well and more than 5 dug wells were closed. The
   abstraction regime is provoking subsidence. The soil compaction is
   affecting the urban and industrial infrastructure. Part of the urban
   area is been divided in two blocks. The 50 similar to 60 cm step is also
   breaking water pipelines and sewage. Subsidence is altering aquifer
   vulnerability. A radon monitoring is also carrying out to analysis the
   tectonic framework of the area. The role of the subsidence fractures in
   aquifer vulnerability assessment techniques like DRASTIC and AVI is
   analyzed. Keywords: DRASTIC, AVI, aquifer vulnerability.},
