Abstract = {This work estimates the total spectral atmospheric transmission in the
   urban environment of Athens on four selected days, one in each season.
   based on a radiative transfer model. With records of spectral direct
   solar irradiance measurements in the spectral range of 310-575 nm, the
   partial spectral atmospheric transmission functions due to Rayleigh and
   aerosol scattering, ozone, nitrogen oxide, mixed gases and water vapour
   absorption are provided. The results are discussed in view of the
   weather conditions prevailing during the selected days of measurements.},
