   Educ \& Ciencia; Inst Agua \& Ciencias Ambientales; Univ Alicante, Grupo
   Invest Modelizac Matemat Sistemas},
Abstract = {The remarkable development of reuse of water in Spain has taken place
   not only because of the necessity to extend water supplies, but also due
   to the requirements to improve the management in water treatment. Water
   supply consumption has increased, along with the increase of population
   that has taken place in numerous urban zones. As a result, traditional
   supplying sources are insufficient to satisfy the demand, which is in
   permanent expansion. This paper will analyze from an economical point of
   view, the effects of the Directive 91/271/EEC in Spain, as well as the
   new rule that appears in the Order in Council of December 8, 2007 in
   which the legal regime of treated water reuse is established.
   Furthermore, costs of reused and recycled water by means of different
   treatment systems will be discussed, as well as the environmental costs
   associated to them.},
