   Technology (REIT 2010), Int Soc Resource Environm Informat Technol,
   Kaifeng, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 19-21, 2010},
Organization = {Int Soc Resource Environm Informat Technol},
Abstract = {Roads are conspicuous components of landscapes and play a substantial
   role in affecting spatial distribution of construction land. Qichun
   County was taken for a case study, we analyzed the influence scope of
   road with the same level on construction land of different types and the
   influence intensity of roads with different levels on construction land
   of the same type, in which the influence scope of national and
   provincial highway on urban land and rural land were 800m and 200m
   separately, and it had no significant effect on industrial and mining
   land. The influence scope of county road on urban land, rural land and
   industrial and mining land were 500m, 200m and 275m respectively. There
   was no obvious correlation between expressway and spatial distribution
   of construction land. The influence intensity of national and provincial
   highway on construction land was stronger than county road. Dividing the
   influence scopes into five levels of significant affected zone,
   remarkable affected zone, general affected zone, weak affected zone and
   extremely weak affected zone. Our results are important for
   understanding the impacts of roads on construction land, and can be
   provided as a case support for relevant planning and researches.},
