Organization = {Taylors Port; Centro Ciencia Vivo Algarve; Centro Invest Espaco
   Organizacoes; Fundacao Calouste Gulbenkian; Espaco Aberto; Delta;
   Alportel; FCT},
Abstract = {In modern cities, people generally have the desire to strike a proper
   balance between man and nature. This paper alms to discuss the method of
   using topographic formations in landscape design, particularly focusing
   on three topographic functions: enclosure forming, viewpoint settings,
   and view settings. We selected Japanese gardens as case studies and
   adopted a three-layer model to classify a landscape design based on
   topographic functions, site planning, and architectural planning. In
   Jyojyu-in, the unique topographic condition is utilized to form an
   enclosed space and to realize both a deep mountain view and a prospect
   view. In Jisho-ji, the unique topographic condition is utilized to form
   an enclosed space and construct three different views.},
