   Univ; New York Acad Sci; European Soc Cognit Sci Music},
Abstract = {Mismatch negativity (MMN) was used to investigate the processing of the
   discrimination between native and non-native CV syllables in tonal
   languages. MMN elicited by the native word was greater than that
   elicited by the non-native word. Hearing a native-language deviant
   significantly altered the elicited MMN in both amplitude and scalp
   voltage field distribution, reflecting the presence of a long-term
   memory trace for spoken words in tonal languages.},
