   - Perspectives from Business in Asia, Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV
   17, 2006},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Hong Kong Univ, Ctr Urban Planning \& Environm
   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {Industrializing countries and post-industrializing countries are in
   different industrializing periods. Because of the variance of economic
   development, technology, integrity of regulation systems, public
   environmental consciousness, the two has many differences in terms of
   circular economy construction. The circular economy of
   post-industrializing countries is initiative, while circular economy of
   industrializing countries is passive. Although there are some
   similarities between the two, profits in industrializing countries are
   much less that their developed European counterparts. In reality, it's
   the government that takes the action of circular economy due to resource
   restriction, environment pollution and industrial upgrading pressure.
   This article suggests building a circular economy evaluation system in
   accordance with the characteristics of China. In addition, the author
   brings out a district circular economy evaluation system with a method
   of identifying the evaluating exponent.},
