Note = {12th Conference on Medicine Meets Virtual Reality, Newport Beach, CA,
   JAN 15-17, 2004},
Abstract = {Vision loss is common among people over the age of 65 and the condition
   is irreversible in most cases. Our simulator is a means to effectively
   and accurately inform people about the nature of common vision problems,
   initially limited to medically accurate simulations of cataract and
   macular degeneration. Using an eye tracker that continuously determines
   the subject's fixation point, a systematically degraded digital image
   displayed on an HMD can be a powerful educational tool. This article
   presents our Virtual Vision Loss (VVL) simulator and the developed
   simulation techniques based on calibration from 27 subjects.},
