Abstract = {It is now largely admitted that cultural heritage could be considered a
   set of tangible and intangible assets, which are developed, transmitted,
   processed to enhance the identity and also the economical situation of a
   territory. Yet, in Algeria, cultural heritage has rarely been considered
   as a resource. After being considered as a conservation tool and as an
   essential constitution of the nation, cultural heritage has become a
   resource for the construction and development of territories. This paper
   is based on a doctorate research and analyses cultural heritage from an
