   (SC), Alicante, SPAIN, 2016},
Organization = {Wessex Inst; Univ Alicante; WIT Transact Ecol \& Environm; Int Journal
   Sustainable Dev \& Planning; Int Journal Design \& Nat \& Ecodynam},
Abstract = {Since the early eighties, tourism has become the dominant axis of
   economic development in the city of Cabo San Lucas. The aim of this
   paper is to develop an analytical framework to assess the impact of
   tourism on the local sustainable development of Cabo San Lucas. The
   methodology applied is analytical-descriptive, based on economic,
   social, demographic, and urban infrastructure variables. The temporary
   evaluation corresponds to the period 1990-2015. The quantitative
   analysis is complemented by qualitative information obtained from focus
   groups (group approach) to identify the valuation of local tourism
   performance by main stake-holders in the area.
   The results allow to identify a number of imbalances and deficits
   currently affecting the city; for example, the accelerated process of
   immigration, coupled with an urban sprawl, promotes important lags in
   urban and social infrastructure. At the same time, the lack of a
   diversified productive base, capable of providing alternative employment
   and income, is generating excessive pressure on natural resources for
   tourism, which alienates this city from a model for sustainable tourism
   development.},
